  "higgsfield_feature": "AI Director",
  "notes": "Agent notes. Every input is optional: an empty media slot is ignored. Two ways to drive the Material Planner. (1) Simple: global_prompt + duration (seconds per segment) + segment_count + optional segment_prompts (one prompt per line); the builder splits the duration into equal H3-legal windows and assigns every picture/audio to every segment. (2) Exact: segment_windows, a JSON string {\"windows\":[{\"start\":0,\"end\":192,\"prompt\":\"shot\",\"images\":[0],\"audios\":[0]}],\"videos\":[{\"index\":0,\"start\":0,\"duration\":5,\"trimStart\":0,\"referenceMode\":\"guide\"}],\"audios\":[{\"index\":0,\"start\":0,\"duration\":5,\"trimStart\":0}]}. Frames are 24 fps, each window length should be 5+17n, windows may overlap (default 39-frame seam). images/audios are 0-based indices into image1..image9 / audio1..audio3; videos are timeline clips indexed into video1..video3 and are sliced per segment by their time window. Files go through run_app.files (absolute paths) under the ids image1..image9, video1..video3, audio1..audio3. audio_mode=locked keeps the source waveform, video_audio carries the videos' sound. two_stage + upscaler + high_steps enable SelfLift. detail is the sparse-attention sparsity (0.9 fast … 0.5 detailed). With an empty media bin, leave images/audios empty in every window: the graph then runs pure text-to-video. Pair the FL2VA DiT with the Pika Flex FL2VA LoRA; the Pika app's flex_mode select does this pairing for you. The 4-step adapter also drives 6-step sampling; RelayVSR x2/x4 can be selected in the Production profile and is applied to the final clip. Qwen3.8 Heretic prompt enhancement is enabled by default; it rewrites every Material Planner segment in order, feeding previous scenes as context and using each segment's ordered pictures/clips.",
